### Payment Service API Tests
### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Create Payment Intent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/create-payment-intent
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "amount": 1000,
  "currency": "usd",
  "orderId": null,
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Test payment for game server"
  }
}

### 2. Create Payment Intent with Order ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/create-payment-intent
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "amount": 2999,
  "currency": "usd",
  "orderId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "metadata": {
    "server_plan": "Premium",
    "quantity": "1"
  }
}

### 3. Confirm Payment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/confirm-payment
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "paymentIntentId": "pi_test_123456789",
  "paymentMethodId": "pm_card_visa"
}

### 4. Refund Payment (Full Refund)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/refund
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "paymentIntentId": "pi_test_123456789",
  "reason": "Customer request"
}

### 5. Refund Payment (Partial Refund)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/refund
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "paymentIntentId": "pi_test_123456789",
  "amount": 500,
  "reason": "Partial refund for service issue"
}

### 6. Create Checkout Session (Existing Endpoint)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/create-checkout-session
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "serverPlanId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "quantity": 1
}

### 7. Get Checkout Session (Existing Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/checkout-session/cs_test_123456789
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Webhook Endpoint (No Auth Required)
### Note: This is typically called by Stripe, not directly by clients
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/stripe
Content-Type: application/json
Stripe-Signature: whsec_test_secret

{
  "id": "evt_test_webhook",
  "object": "event",
  "type": "payment_intent.succeeded",
  "data": {
    "object": {
      "id": "pi_test_123456789",
      "amount": 1000,
      "currency": "usd",
      "status": "succeeded"
    }
  }
}

###
### Testing Instructions
###
### 1. First, authenticate and get a JWT token:
###    - Use the auth endpoints to login
###    - Copy the token from the response
###    - Replace YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE with your actual token
###
### 2. Test Create Payment Intent:
###    - Run test #1 to create a basic payment intent
###    - Save the paymentIntentId and clientSecret from response
###
### 3. Test Confirm Payment (in real scenario):
###    - Use Stripe.js on frontend to collect payment method
###    - Send payment method ID to confirm endpoint
###    - For testing, you can use test payment method IDs
###
### 4. Test Refund:
###    - Use a successfully completed payment intent ID
###    - Test both full and partial refunds
###
### 5. Webhook Testing:
###    - Use Stripe CLI for local webhook testing:
###      stripe listen --forward-to localhost:5000/api/webhooks/stripe
###    - Trigger test webhooks:
###      stripe trigger payment_intent.succeeded
###
### Test Card Numbers (for Stripe test mode):
### - Success: 4242 4242 4242 4242
### - Declined: 4000 0000 0000 0002
### - 3D Secure: 4000 0027 6000 3184
### - Any future expiry date and any 3-digit CVC
